.\" Manual page for docmost-cli-space(1)
.\" Source: SPECIFICATION.md section 4.3, src/docmost_cli/cli/space.py
.TH DOCMOST\-CLI\-SPACE 1 "2026\-03\-22" "docmost\-cli 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
docmost\-cli\-space \- manage Docmost wiki spaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B docmost\-cli space list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli space create
.BI \-\-name " name"
.RB [ \-\-slug
.IR slug ]
.RB [ \-\-description
.IR desc ]
.br
.B docmost\-cli space update
.I space\-slug
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-description
.IR desc ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commands for managing Docmost wiki spaces.
Spaces are top\-level organizational containers for pages.
Each space has a unique slug used to identify it in CLI commands.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS list
List all spaces in the workspace.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Maximum total number of results across all pages.
When omitted, every page is retrieved.
.TP
.BI \-\-page\-size " N"
Results per request, 1\-100. Default: 100.
.TP
.BI \-\-cursor " cursor"
Fetch a single page of results starting at this cursor.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-follow
Fetch a single page of results instead of following pagination.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output as a JSON array.
Each element is the complete object the server returned, not just the table
columns.
.TP
.BI \-\-fields " a,b,c"
Comma\-separated list of fields to output.
Applies to both
.B \-\-json
and the table, replacing the default columns.
Names are matched against the fields the server returned; an unknown name is a
usage error listing what is available.
.TP
.B \-\-envelope
With
.BR \-\-json ,
wrap the results as
.B {"items": [...], "meta": {...}}
so the caller can read
.B hasNextPage
and
.BR nextCursor .
.PP
Default table columns: id, name, slug, description.
These affect the table only; \-\-json emits every field the server returns.
.SS create
Create a new space.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Space display name.
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-slug " slug"
URL slug for the space.
Auto\-generated from the name if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-description " description"
Space description.
.PP
Outputs the new space ID to stdout.
.SS update
Update an existing space's name or description.
.PP
.I space\-slug
is a positional argument identifying the space to update.
At least one of
.B \-\-name
or
.B \-\-description
must be provided.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
New space name.
.TP
.BI \-\-description " description"
New space description.
.SH EXAMPLES
List all spaces:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli space list
.EE
.RE
.PP
List spaces as JSON:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli space list \-\-json | jq \(aq.[].slug\(aq
.EE
.RE
.PP
Create a space with a custom slug:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli space create \-\-name "Engineering" \-\-slug eng
.EE
.RE
.PP
Update a space description:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ docmost\-cli space update eng \-\-description "Engineering team docs"
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
See
.BR docmost\-cli (1).
